 "power": "3.3V logic; GPIOs are not 5V tolerant, divide 5V module signals. The 5V pin is USB pass-through.",
 "flash_how": "Flash straight over the USB-C data cable: pio run -t upload. CH340 serial chip; upload_speed 115200 is the safe choice (921600 gives Unable to verify flash chip connection). Usually no need to press BOOT.",
 "gotchas": [
  "36/39/34/35 are input-only, no pinMode OUTPUT",
  "GPIO0/2/12/15 are strapping pins; the onboard LED on 2 is fine, do not add a pull-up on 12",
  "ADC2 pins (0/2/4/12-15/25-27) do not work while WiFi is on; prefer 32-39 for analog",
  "UART0 (1/3) is used by USB flashing, leave it alone"
